    "summary": "Alligator jam roars, Lovelight sequence shines in relaxed Fillmore set",
    "blurb": "The second set erupts with a monster Alligator jam followed by a seamless Turn On Your Lovelight → Not Fade Away → Lovelight sequence. Pigpen’s organ on Lovelight is highlighted and the drumming throughout is superb. Highlights also include New Orleans and the classic China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider pairing.",
    "review": "June 6, 1970 at Fillmore West captured one of the band’s most relaxed yet adventurous evenings. After a solid acoustic opener that featured a standout Frozen Logger and crisp Friend Of The Devil, the second set launched into an hour‑long improvisational odyssey. Jerry’s soaring lead on the Alligator jam is pure fire, weaving through thunderous Bill Kreutzmann drums and a tight partnership with Bob that kept the momentum rolling. The Lovelight sequence – Turn On Your Lovelight into Not Fade Away back into Lovelight – showcases Pigpen’s organ in full Janis‑Joplin swagger, while the dual‑drum section adds an extra layer of drive. Classic moments like China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider and the raucous New Orleans jam further cement this show as a high‑vibe snapshot of the Dead at peak summer ’70 form. The soundboard recordings are consistently praised for clarity, with the bear‑latvala capture standing out as the most pristine, delivering every nuance without hiss or drop‑outs.",
